  "summary": "Carlos Chagas was a Brazilian physician born near Oliveira, Minas Gerais, in 1878 and died in Rio de Janeiro in 1934. In 1909 he identified American trypanosomiasis, later called Chagas disease, and named its agent Trypanosoma cruzi in honour of Oswaldo Cruz.",
